{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "a1b2c3d4-e5f6-7890-abcd-ef1234567890",
    "name": "Cloud AI Commerce Platform",
    "description": "API collection for commerce platform microservices.\n\n## Auth tokens\n\n1. **Login** — saves `accessToken` (JWT) and `refreshToken` (opaque) to collection + environment.\n2. **Refresh Token** — when the JWT expires, call refresh with `{{refreshToken}}`; response rotates both tokens (store the new `refreshToken`).\n3. **Validate Token** — checks the current `accessToken`.\n\n## Authorization header\n\nCollection pre-request script adds `Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}` when a token exists. Public routes (`/login`, `/refresh`, `/health`) ignore it. **Validate Token (missing token)** strips Authorization on purpose.\n\nRe-import after collection updates.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "auth": {
    "type": "bearer",
    "bearer": [
      {
        "key": "token",
        "value": "{{accessToken}}",
        "type": "string"
      }
    ]
  },
  "event": [
    {
      "listen": "prerequest",
      "script": {
        "type": "text/javascript",
        "exec": [
          "const token = pm.collectionVariables.get('accessToken')",
          "    || (pm.environment ? pm.environment.get('accessToken') : '');",
          "",
          "if (token) {",
          "    pm.request.headers.upsert({",
          "        key: 'Authorization',",
          "        value: 'Bearer ' + token",
          "    });",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "authServiceBaseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": "",
      "type": "string"
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Auth Service",
      "description": "Recommended order: **Login** → **Refresh Token** (when JWT expires) → **Validate Token**.\n\nVariables: `accessToken` (Bearer JWT), `refreshToken` (body for `/refresh` only).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/health",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "health"]
            },
            "description": "Sends Bearer token automatically after Login (API does not require it). Check **Headers** tab for `Authorization`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    const token = json.accessToken;",
                  "    const refresh = json.refreshToken;",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', token);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', refresh);",
                  "    if (pm.environment) {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('accessToken', token);",
                  "        pm.environment.set('refreshToken', refresh);",
                  "    }",
                  "    pm.test('accessToken saved for entire collection', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(token).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    });",
                  "    pm.test('refreshToken saved for refresh endpoint', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(refresh).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    });",
                  "    console.log('accessToken updated — next requests will send Authorization header.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"vincent\",\n  \"password\": \"123456\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Run first (or to get a new session). On success, saves `accessToken` and `refreshToken`.\n\nWhen the JWT expires (~1h), use **Refresh Token** instead of logging in again.\n\nSample users: `vincent` / `admin` / `tester` — password `123456`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "    const json = pm.response.json();",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "    pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "    if (pm.environment) {",
                  "        pm.environment.set('accessToken', json.accessToken);",
                  "        pm.environment.set('refreshToken', json.refreshToken);",
                  "    }",
                  "    pm.test('tokens rotated', function () {",
                  "        pm.expect(json.accessToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "        pm.expect(json.refreshToken).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
                  "    });",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Run after **Login** when `accessToken` is expired or before it expires to rotate refresh token.\n\n- Request body: `{ \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\" }` (no Bearer required).\n- On 200: overwrites `accessToken` and `refreshToken` — always use the latest refresh value.\n- Reusing an old refresh token returns 401."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh Token (invalid)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"not-a-valid-refresh-token\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/refresh",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "refresh"]
            },
            "description": "Expected HTTP 401 with message `Invalid refresh token`."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Login (invalid credentials)",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"username\": \"vincent\",\n  \"password\": \"wrong-password\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/login",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "login"]
            },
            "description": "Also sends Bearer if token exists. Expected HTTP 401."
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate Token",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/validate",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "validate"]
            },
            "description": "Requires valid `accessToken` from **Login** or **Refresh Token**. Expected: `{ \"valid\": true, ... }`"
          },
          "response": []
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate Token (missing token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "prerequest",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.request.headers.remove('Authorization');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{authServiceBaseUrl}}/api/v1/auth/validate",
              "host": ["{{authServiceBaseUrl}}"],
              "path": ["api", "v1", "auth", "validate"]
            },
            "description": "Only request that **strips** Authorization (for testing 401). Expected HTTP 401."
          },
          "response": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
